section: compiler
synopsis: Cmm procedures can declare the CPU features they require
description:
  A hand-written Cmm procedure may now carry a target attribute,
  ``__attribute__((target("avx2")))``, saying which CPU features it needs.
  This is a property of the code, not a build option: ``stg_ap_v32_fast``
  cannot be compiled correctly without AVX2, while ``stg_ap_v16_fast`` in the
  same library must not be compiled with AVX at all. The RTS uses this in place
  of Hadrian's per-file flags, which had to be matched on filename.

  A backend that cannot honour the attribute rejects it, and an unrecognised
  feature is a parse error. See ``Note [Cmm target attributes]`` in ``GHC.Cmm``.
